{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-exact-pairing","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:glossary-exact-pairing","kind":"remark","title":"Exact pairing","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-glossary-monoidal-category"],"tags":["glossary","category-theory","monoidal","duality"],"text":"glossary-exact-pairing.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:glossary-exact-pairing\"></a><p><strong><a class=\"refterm\" href=\"#term-exact-pairing\">Exact pairing</a>.</strong> Given objects <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Y</code> in a monoidal category, an exact pairing consists of morphisms <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\varepsilon \\colon X \\otimes Y \\to \\mathbf{1}</code> (evaluation) and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\eta \\colon \\mathbf{1} \\to Y \\otimes X</code> (coevaluation) satisfying the snake identities:</p>\n<p><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\varepsilon \\otimes \\mathrm{id}_X) \\circ (\\mathrm{id}_X \\otimes \\eta) = \\mathrm{id}_X, \\qquad (\\mathrm{id}_Y \\otimes \\varepsilon) \\circ (\\eta \\otimes \\mathrm{id}_Y) = \\mathrm{id}_Y.</code></p>\n<p>When an exact pairing exists, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Y</code> is a right dual of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">X</code> a left dual of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Y</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/notation/glossary-exact-pairing.md","heading":"Remark","number":"30.2.6","page":"b/rem-glossary-exact-pairing","qa":{"counts":{"pass":60,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":17,"unknown":0,"stale":60},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
